{# One key per line, which is the only thing sshd accepts. Written as a template
   rather than as `content:` in the task, after a YAML lesson worth keeping: a
   double-quoted scalar that spans source lines folds those line breaks into
   spaces, so `join('\n')` written across two lines joined the keys with a space
   and put them all on one line. sshd then read the first key and treated
   everything after it, including a whole RSA key, as its comment. The ed25519
   worked, the RSA silently did not, and nothing anywhere reported an error. #}
{% for key in workstation_user_authorized_keys %}
{{ key }}
{% endfor %}
